~ map_002
Zaar: These look different.

Aven: They are captains. Which is absurd.

Zaar: Why?

Aven: Well, by now we should have encountered a few sergeants and maybe one or two lieutenants. So we skipped a few ranks. And I would not call their control efficient.

Zaar: Maybe after hundreds of years they became dumber?

Aven: Underestimate them at your own peril.
=> END

~ map_003
Aven: SO these are the creatures that you were talking about?

Alastor: Yes, Archchancellor. They are clearly otherworldly.

Elliot: Although, this time something is different.

Alastor: Yes. This time around I don't feel such a strong pull towards their eradication. … Archchancellor? Zaar? Are you alright?

Aven: Listen to my order. Rid this world of their presence!

Zaar: Gladly.
=> END

~ map_004
Zaar: Didn't see that one before.

Alastor: Careful. I think it's about to do something.

///

Zaar: WHAT.

Alastor: I sensed no magic! What is this nonsense!

Elliot: Guess we now know where these creatures came from.

Alastor: So it just creates them?

Aven: Copies. That's what I was missing. Now the puzzle pieces fit together. All the servants that we have encountered were clones.

Zaar: Let's finish this one off before it makes more.
=> END

~ map_005
Zaar: We were in a cave, right?

Elliot: Right.

Zaar: And now we are in some kind of void, with flying islands and an eyesore of an environment.

Elliot: Correct.

Zaar: What in the Saint's name is going on?

Alastor: You know she actually has a name, and it's

Zaar: I DON'T CARE. WHERE ARE WE?

Aven: If I were to borrow the terminology of a certain mage, we are inside the Dragon, as we always were.

Zaar: Great! An answer that raises more questions that it answers.

Aven: One can say that we traveled to another world or shifted dimensions. I would say that we left normality and entered a realm from which these abominations entered ours.

Zaar: Are we at least getting closer to our goal?

Aven: Without a doubt.
=> END

